My point was that the incremental value of having early
DSM/MR/reflection from Minetown through the castle is far greater than
the value of having a permanent light source.  More than enough to
offset the 20% chance of not getting it.  The key to ascending at a
high ration is to eliminate instadeaths ruthlessly.

There are very few chances of a permanent light source, but having a
_permanent_ light source isn't necessary, nor as helpful as people are
making it out to be--you can get all of the benefits of light without
necessarily having a permanent source.  And in the short term, you will
have the lamp for immediate needs.

Burning a wish on a magic marker can get you thousands of turns of
light as well as a bunch of AC and other niceties.

You're right that you need to be rigorous about turning off the lamp
when you're wandering around lit levels.

Believe me, I'm very aware of the benefits of light.  I'm one of the
camp that values jumping boots over speed boots, and light is mandatory
to take full advantage of them.  But there are plenty of resources to
ensure that you have light going forward, except possibly a gap between
when the initial lamp runs out and you reach the castle (assuming there
was only the 1 lamp and you haven't found potions of oil, etc).  That's
a bummer, for sure, and if I could have the wish and the lamp I'd love
to.  But early on, the value of that wish is _huge_.



